# Cardtype empty-group separator: issue 164

## Request and change

Preserve the original Ruby grouped-list mapping's empty position when Custom
has no items, restoring the missing LF before Organize. Keep group contents,
permission decisions and normalization unchanged; keep this correction separate
from issues 154 and 156.

The sole production hunk changes `groupedListView` in
`src/card/mod-loader/mods/card-mod-rules.ts`. Its loop previously continued
without adding an output position for an empty group. Ruby's documented
`map { ...; next if type_list.empty?; ... }.flatten.join "\n"` retains the
nil position and therefore its separator. The loop now pushes an empty string
before continuing. Nonempty groups follow the identical existing path.

No group arrays, listing contents, deny logic, preparation paths, drivers,
normalizers or issue154/156 production files changed. No private page data is
included in the test or report.

